From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cmatte <cmatte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the broker's acl_file decide after an ACL grant

On Mosquitto 2.1 the ACL check runs through every registered plugin
callback in order and stops at the first result that is not
MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_DEFER or MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE. The broker's own
acl_file check is registered after the plugins, so when go-auth grants
access with MOSQ_ERR_SUCCESS the acl_file is never consulted.

Return MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE for a grant instead, so a configured
acl_file can still restrict access. Without an acl_file every callback
ignores and the broker allows the request, as before. Denials and
errors are unchanged, and older Mosquitto versions keep returning
MOSQ_ERR_SUCCESS.
---
 auth-plugin.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/auth-plugin.c b/auth-plugin.c
index fc45f26..d29f174 100644
--- a/auth-plugin.c
+++ b/auth-plugin.c
@@ -133,7 +133,13 @@ int mosquitto_auth_acl_check(void *userdata, const char *clientid, const char *u
   switch (ret)
   {
   case AuthGranted:
+#if defined(LIBMOSQUITTO_VERSION_NUMBER) && LIBMOSQUITTO_VERSION_NUMBER >= 2001000
+    /* Mosquitto 2.1+: a grant does not end the check; later checks
+     * (e.g. the broker's own acl_file) still decide. */
+    return MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE;
+#else
     return MOSQ_ERR_SUCCESS;
+#endif
     break;
   case AuthRejected:
     return MOSQ_ERR_ACL_DENIED;
